  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RESTORATION OF FRESHWATER WETLANDS AS WA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project proposes to restore, enhance and protect 1,077 acres of these freshwater wetlands in collaboration with landowners to help meet the objectives established by the North American Wetland Management Plan. ..The Laguna Madre and its inland freshwater wetlands are a Mexican Priority Wetland and a Key Wetland for Shorebirds and Waterbirds. It provides key habitat to migratory and resident waterfowl species such as redhead, northern pintail, blue-winged teal, cinnamon teal, lesser scaup, mottled duck, masked duck, Muscovy duck, snow goose, white-fronted goose and Ross&apos;s snow goose. ..</narrative>
  </description>
